Pre-parsing: Save serialised AST output after parsing source files with MD5(?) hash of the source file in the name. We have 2 parsers, so we would need to include the parser variant in the file name too. For example, parsing .../path-to/array.rb would be named .../path-to/.array.<SHA>.wq.ast or .../path-to/.array.<SHA>.prism.ast. We probably don't want these polluting the source tree, so maybe under ~/.frozone/ast/ directory. Then for load we take the hash of the source file, look for a preparsed file, deserialize it if it already exists, otherwise parse (again) and save the serialized AST.

